// Title: Potentially Suspicious JWT Token Search Via CLI
// Sigma ID: 6d3a3952-6530-44a3-8554-cf17c116c615
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), kagebunsher
// Date: 2022-10-25 | Modified: 2025-10-21
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1528, T1552.001
// Description: Detects potentially suspicious search for JWT tokens via CLI by looking for the string "eyJ0eX"
//   or "eyJhbG". JWT tokens are often used for access-tokens across various applications and
//   services like Microsoft 365, Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, and others. Threat actors may search for
//   these tokens to steal them for lateral movement or privilege escalation.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://mrd0x.com/stealing-tokens-from-office-applications/
//   - https://www.scip.ch/en/?labs.20240523
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_jwt_token_search.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "find " or ProcessCommandLine contains "find.exe" or ProcessCommandLine contains "findstr" or ProcessCommandLine contains "select-string " or ProcessCommandLine contains "strings") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "eyJ0eXAiOi" or ProcessCommandLine contains "eyJhbGciOi" or ProcessCommandLine contains " eyJ0eX" or ProcessCommandLine contains " \"eyJ0eX\"" or ProcessCommandLine contains " 'eyJ0eX'" or ProcessCommandLine contains " eyJhbG" or ProcessCommandLine contains " \"eyJhbG\"" or ProcessCommandLine contains " 'eyJhbG'")
